                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "To avoid seeming, at best, hopelessly old-fashioned, you should generally steer clear of gender-specific nouns. Here are two rules of thumb:",
            "block_bbox": [
                91,
                1092,
                783,
                1143
            ],
            "block_id": 13,
            "block_order": 12,
            "group_id": 13,
            "global_block_id": 13,
            "global_group_id": 13,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    91.0,
                    1092.0
                ],
                [
                    783.0,
                    1092.0
                ],
                [
                    783.0,
                    1143.0
                ],
                [
                    91.0,
                    1143.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "- Avoid using nouns gendered as feminine when their counterparts are not explicitly gendered masculine. Use the formerly masculine noun for all genders or find an alternative. A woman who tells jokes for a living is not",
